The C++ provider selects formatting, layout, and project kind independently. The CLI catalogs are `rivet styles` and `rivet layouts`.

## Formatting presets

Rivet writes the chosen `BasedOnStyle` to `.clang-format`. The Neovim wizard uses the installed `clang-format` to preview a sample when available; CLI previews are illustrative. Exact output follows that formatter's version and [style options](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/ClangFormatStyleOptions.html).

| Preset | Typical formatting |
| --- | --- |
| `LLVM` | Compact, two-space indentation; Rivet's default |
| `Google` | Two-space indentation, compact braces |
| `Chromium` | Google-derived formatting with Chromium conventions |
| `Mozilla` | Two spaces, function braces on separate lines |
| `WebKit` | Four spaces, function braces on separate lines |
| `Microsoft` | Four spaces, expanded braces |
| `GNU` | Indented braces, spaces before call parentheses |

Rivet sets `.editorconfig` indentation to four spaces for WebKit/Microsoft and two for the other presets. These presets control formatting; broader coding conventions belong in the project's contribution guide.

## Layouts

| Layout | Starting organization |
| --- | --- |
| `feature` (default) | Application in `app/`, co-located core files in `src/core/`, tests in `tests/` |
| `library` | Public headers in `include/<name>/`, implementations in `src/`, module interfaces in `modules/` |
| `flat` | Main, core, and test files at the project root |

Application files exist only for application projects. The module/header choice determines which interface files are generated. Additional file placement is described in [Files and targets](/docs/templates/).

## Project kinds

| Kind | Generated targets |
| --- | --- |
| `app` (default) | Application, reusable static core library, CTest executable |
| `library` | Static library, CTest executable |

Either kind supports all three layouts. A directory does not create a target; target boundaries are explicit.

```sh
rivet new geometry --kind library --layout library \
  --modules false --header-guard ifndef --style WebKit --preview
```

This previews a static C++ library using public headers and WebKit formatting. Workload dependencies are selected separately through [parallel](/docs/hpc/) or [graphics](/docs/graphics/) profiles.
